---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { site } from '../lib/site.mjs';
---
<Layout title="Privacy Policy" description="What Biology Lab collects and why: no accounts, Google Analytics usage statistics, Adsterra banner ads, and practice scores kept only in your browser." schemaType="Article"><article class="article"><div class="eyebrow">Privacy</div><h1>Privacy Policy</h1><p><em>Last updated: October 21, 2026</em></p><p>Biology Lab ({site.url.replace('https://', '')}) is free to use and never asks you to sign up. This page explains, in plain language, what information is collected when you visit, who collects it, and how you can opt out.</p><h2>No accounts, no forms</h2><p>There are no accounts, logins, or sign-up forms, so we never ask for your name or email address. Everything you type into a calculator, including any DNA sequence, is processed on your own device and is not sent to our servers.</p><h2>Usage statistics (Google Analytics)</h2><p>We use Google Analytics ({site.analyticsId}) to count visits and see which pages and tools are used, so we know what to improve. Google Analytics uses cookies and similar technology to collect information such as the pages you view, how long you stay, the referring site, your approximate location, and your device and browser type. Calculator inputs and practice answers are not sent to Google Analytics. Read <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites">how Google uses information from sites that use its services</a>.</p><h2>Advertising (Adsterra)</h2><p>A small number of banner ads help keep the lab free. They are served by Adsterra and load only when you scroll near them. There are no pop-ups, pop-unders, or full-screen ads, and ads never appear inside a calculator.</p><p>To show ads, limit how often you see the same one, measure results, and prevent fraud, Adsterra and its advertising partners may use cookies, pixels, or similar identifiers. They may receive your IP address, browser and device details, and the address of the page you are viewing. Their use of this information is covered by <a href="https://adsterra.com/privacy-policy-managed">Adsterra’s Privacy Policy</a> and <a href="https://adsterra.com/cookies/">Cookies Policy</a>.</p><h2>Saved in your browser</h2><p>Your best practice scores are saved in your browser’s local storage so you can see your progress next time. They never leave your device, and clearing your browser data removes them.</p><h2>Other services</h2><p>Fonts load from Google Fonts, and our hosting provider keeps standard access logs (such as IP address and requested page) to deliver the site and protect it from abuse.</p><h2>Your choices</h2><ul><li><strong>Cookies:</strong> block or delete cookies in your browser settings. The tools keep working without them.</li><li><strong>Ads:</strong> use your browser’s tracking protection or an ad blocker.</li><li><strong>Analytics:</strong> install the <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout">Google Analytics opt-out browser add-on</a>.</li><li><strong>Practice scores:</strong> clear this site’s data in your browser.</li></ul><h2>Students</h2><p>Biology Lab is made for students and does not ask anyone for personal information. Parents and teachers with questions are welcome to contact us.</p><h2>Changes and contact</h2><p>If anything here changes, we will update this page and the date at the top. Questions about privacy? Email <a href={`mailto:${site.contactEmail}`}>{site.contactEmail}</a>.</p><div class="related"><a href="/about/">About Biology Lab ↗</a><a href="/">Explore the tools ↗</a></div></article></Layout>
